.TH WAVE-INSTALL 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-install \- Install a package, or one specific version of it. Several packages can be given at once, separated by commas; each may carry its own @version.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave install <package>[@<version>] [, <package>[@<version>] ...] [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install a package, or one specific version of it. Several packages can
be given at once, separated by commas; each may carry its own @version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-continue
Resume an interrupted download
.TP
.B \-\-proxy <string>
HTTP/HTTPS proxy (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080)
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-ssl
Skip SSL certificate verification (insecure)
.TP
.B \-\-limit\-rate <string>
Limit download speed (e.g. 200K, 1M, 5M; a bare number means bytes)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-time <string>
Maximum total time for one request (40s, 1min, 1min20s, 2h; a bare
number means seconds)
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-timeout <string>
Maximum time for the handshake
.TP
.B \-\-content\-time <string>
Maximum time to receive data
.TP
.B \-\-no\-link
Do not touch the unversioned link (the old name --unlink still works)
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-force
Install anyway when the running macOS is older than the package declares
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Plain output for logs and scripts: no emoji, no colours, ASCII progress
bar
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Verbose mode

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave install jq
wave install ffmpeg@6.1
wave install jq, yq, fx@40.0.2
wave install jq,yq
wave install jq --limit-rate 1M
wave install jq --max-time=1min
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
